                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "developmentalism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51aa69e4-9888-30b7-b043-ae8609a81a9b",
                                        "entry_id": "c89ce75b-d8ba-3d74-bf38-e48b0f3f0cff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An economic theory which states that the best way for Third World countries to develop is through fostering a strong and varied internal market and imposing high tariffs on imported goods."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2d8cf46-dc99-40cd-8c80-fe7534e144db",
                                                "sense_id": "51aa69e4-9888-30b7-b043-ae8609a81a9b",
                                                "text": "Most fundamentally, Sachs argues, developmentalism advocates the wrong values. Under developmentalism, the economy dominates society rather than the more rational opposite."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24d3c97b-7e38-4f88-9f10-3ff3df0278ee",
                                                "sense_id": "51aa69e4-9888-30b7-b043-ae8609a81a9b",
                                                "text": "Nevertheless, the strong political reasons which supported developmentalism had vanished before the World Bank made its diagnosis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce25fc9d-fb42-4332-885e-61dc776dd5bb",
                                                "sense_id": "51aa69e4-9888-30b7-b043-ae8609a81a9b",
                                                "text": "By invoking developmentalism as more than a statist project for economic growth and one that is also led by an imperative to generate well-being among citizens, I focus on the discursive and other practices through which developmentalism is experienced as a condition, a mode of being and a lived experience."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e394e461-901f-4309-9a07-e966fddb1852",
                                                "sense_id": "51aa69e4-9888-30b7-b043-ae8609a81a9b",
                                                "text": "When President Dwight Eisenhower took office in the United States in 1953, he took a decisive stand against developmentalism, which he regarded as a threat to the commercial interests of America's multinational companies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
